            <ArticleTitle>Arthroscopic Arthrodesis of the Distal Tibiofibular Syndesmosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>953-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1053/j.jfas.2015.02.017</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1067-2516(15)00046-0</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chronic syndesmosis disruption can occur if an acute lesion is missed or inadequately managed. This can result in significant functional deficit and development of post-traumatic ankle arthritis. Anatomic reduction of the syndesmosis and maintenance of the reduction by syndesmotic screw fixation alone, ligamentous reconstruction, or fusion of the syndesmosis are recommended. A technique of arthroscopic distal tibiofibular syndesmosis arthrodesis is described.</AbstractText>
